IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cons54-nouns`
IMPORT `cons54-cross-references`

-- Row il-54. The sound citations point at what their words say, and the recorded facts about the three defects and the controls are what NOTES.md says they are.
-- The defects themselves are NOT asserted sound anywhere in this file: their six failing assertions are in cons54-tests-xrefs-red.l4.
-- Every expected value is written from the texts quoted in cons54-cross-references.l4, not from the output of the module.

§ `Tests of the sound citations`

#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(א1), the warranty sticker`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: s 31א(א)(5) to 17ב(ד), the binding price`)
#ASSERT `the citation points at what it says` (`reference: Third Schedule item 1 to the short name, as section 105 rewrites both`)

§ `Tests of what was read from where`

-- Only the Third Schedule control has both limbs read from the official instrument alone (section 105(1) and (2), page 1029).
-- Every other citation has a limb that is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY, either the whole limb or that no later instrument touched the words.
#ASSERT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: Third Schedule item 1 to the short name, as section 105 rewrites both`)
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(א1), the warranty sticker`))
#ASSERT (NOT `both limbs were read from the official instruments` (`reference: s 31א(א)(5) to 17ב(ד), the binding price`))
-- Defect 1 and its control: official pages for both limbs, with the caveat about later instruments.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(א1), the warranty sticker`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(א1), the warranty sticker`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
-- Defect 2: limb (a) as for defect 1; the words of 31א(א)(8) were read from the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- The second control: both limbs are the consolidation only.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(5) to 17ב(ד), the binding price`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(5) to 17ב(ד), the binding price`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the consolidation only`
-- Defect 3: both limbs from the official pages, with the caveat; its control: both from section 105's page alone.
#ASSERT (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instruments read from their page images; that no later instrument touched the words is CONSOLIDATION-ONLY`
#ASSERT (`reference: Third Schedule item 1 to the short name, as section 105 rewrites both`)'s `limb (a) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`
#ASSERT (`reference: Third Schedule item 1 to the short name, as section 105 rewrites both`)'s `limb (b) was read from` EQUALS `the official instrument, read from its page image`

§ `Tests of what the two descriptions of the defects say`

#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the paragraph on warranty certificates, paragraph (5) of subsection (א) of section 18א`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `paragraph (5) of section 18א as a bare address: two paragraphs carry that number, one in subsection (א) and one in subsection (א1), and the section has no paragraph (5) at its top level`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the paragraph on repair and replacement of goods, paragraph (1) of subsection (א) of section 18א`
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `paragraph (1) of section 18א as a bare address: at least three paragraphs carry that number, in subsections (א), (א1) and (ג), and the section has no paragraph (1) at its top level`
#ASSERT (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`)'s `the citing words say it points at` EQUALS `the short name that item 1 of the Second Schedule defines for the Communications Law (Bezeq and Broadcasts), 5742-1982`
#ASSERT (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`)'s `the target is` EQUALS `item 1 of the Second Schedule as section 105 of the Communications (Broadcasts) Law, 5786-2026, rewrites it: it defines a short name for the Bezeq Law and defines no short name for the Communications Law`

§ `Tests of the day the words stop reaching their text`

-- Defects 1 and 2: three months from publication on 26 June 2008 (computed, fork D2); asked only about days well clear of it.
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`) (Date 1 1 2009) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`) (Date 1 1 2009) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- A day before the Amendment: no source held says what the address found then, so NOTHING (fork D1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`) (Date 1 1 2008) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`) (Date 1 1 2008) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Defect 3: two years from publication on 28 July 2026 (computed, fork D2). Today and a day before the rewrite are NOTHING; a day after is FALSE.
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`) (Date 1 1 2030) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`) (Date 1 1 2028) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The controls have no recorded stopping day: NOTHING on any day, which is not a statement that their targets stand.
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(א1), the warranty sticker`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: s 31א(א)(5) to 17ב(ד), the binding price`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the words still reach their text on` (`reference: Third Schedule item 1 to the short name, as section 105 rewrites both`) (Date 10 11 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of the days the citing words start`

-- Sefer HaChukim 3569 p. 913, section 10(א) and (ב)(1): eight months from 22 July 2026, and up to four months more; both computed by this row (fork D2).
#ASSERT (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`)'s `the citing words take effect on before any postponement` EQUALS JUST (Date 22 3 2027)
#ASSERT (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`)'s `the citing words take effect no later than if every postponement is used` EQUALS JUST (Date 22 7 2027)
-- So the Ninth Schedule is in force, even after every postponement, before the short name stops reaching its definition.
#ASSERT `the citing words are in force, even after every postponement, no later than the day their words stop reaching their text` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Sefer HaChukim 2310 p. 1023, section 4(א): 11 Sivan 5772 = 1 June 2012.
#ASSERT (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(א1), the warranty sticker`)'s `the citing words take effect on before any postponement` EQUALS JUST (Date 1 6 2012)
-- Section 105 starts on the day computed above, with the rewrite it makes of the control.
#ASSERT (`reference: Third Schedule item 1 to the short name, as section 105 rewrites both`)'s `the citing words take effect on before any postponement` EQUALS JUST (Date 28 7 2028)
-- No postponement or stopping day is recorded for the defects of the first two kinds: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `the citing words are in force, even after every postponement, no later than the day their words stop reaching their text` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Tests of reading in context`

-- Reading B of the first two defects: read with the words around them, the citing words reach the paragraph they are about. The row records the reading and does not rule on it (fork F1 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the citation reaches what the citing words are about once read in context` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(5), the warranty certificate`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the citation reaches what the citing words are about once read in context` (`reference: s 31א(א)(8) to 18א(1), the repair and replacement`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- The row does not say what a reading in context does for the third defect or the controls: NOTHING (fork F2 in NOTES.md).
#ASSERT `the citation reaches what the citing words are about once read in context` (`reference: Ninth Schedule item 6 to the short name the Second Schedule defines`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the citation reaches what the citing words are about once read in context` (`reference: s 31א(א)(7) to 18א(א1), the warranty sticker`) EQUALS NOTHING
